feat(policy): support Cedar in development builds (#5006)

Add Cedar-authored sandbox policy support behind the `experimental` Cargo
feature flag on `openshell-gateway` and `openshell-supervisor`. Default,
prerelease, and stable builds exclude Cedar.

- Add `CedarPolicy` (tag 7), `provider_credential_rules` (tag 8), and
  `endpoint_settings` (tag 9) to `SandboxPolicy`, plus
  `supported_capabilities` on `SupervisorHello` and `GetSandboxConfigRequest`.
- Keep Cedar parsing, analysis, and evaluation in dedicated crates behind
  `openshell-policy-runtime-interface`, `openshell-policy-cedar-adapter`, and
  `openshell-policy-cedar-runtime`.
- Move cross-backend conformance tests to `tests/policy-conformance`.
- Capture vendored git source replacements for offline RPM builds.

